-- title:
--   Hasse relation: ̄ a₀^{ q}=jmatĥ(s) at a supersingular place
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a nonzero level $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of an algebraic closure of $\mathbb Q$ for which $q$ is a nonunit of $A$; write $\kappa_A$ for its residue field. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC` $\kappa_A\,M'$ over $\kappa_A$ whose members are exactly the supersingular places, i.e. the places $w$ that are rational (the structure map $\kappa_A\to w$'s residue field is onto), are affine geometric, and satisfy $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen})\in \mathrm{ssJSet}\,q$, and fix $s\in W$. Let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar` $M'$ (the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathsf q))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the $q$-expansions $\mathrm{qExpand}\,d\,j$, $d\mid M'$) to `modularFunctionFieldC` $\kappa_A\,M'$, assumed compatible with coefficientwise reduction: every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((\mathsf q))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar` $M'$ is $R_0$-integral, and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa_A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ an element lying in $A$, such that $A\cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$. Let $\ell_g$ be a prime dividing $M'$ and $H_1\le(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ the intersection of $\mathrm{levelH}\,q\,M'$, the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, with the kernel of reduction to $(\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $k_0\subseteq k_0((\mathsf q))$ obtained by base change of the $q$-expansion function field $\mathrm{xHFunctionField}\,(q^2M')\,H_1$ to $k_0$, let $j\in K$ be the element whose Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion $\mathrm{jq}$, with $j\neq 0$, and let $C=\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,(A\cap k_0)\,K\,j$ be the algebra of elements of $K$ integral over $(A\cap k_0)[j]$. Let $y\subset C$ be a maximal ideal containing the image of $\pi_0$, and assume that $y$ lies over $s$ in the following sense: for every $g\in\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M'$ whose base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is $R_0$-integral, such that $g$ has nonnegative order at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar` $M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which $j$ has nonnegative order, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, whenever the coefficientwise image of $g$ lies in $K$ and in $C$, and $c\in k_0$ lies in $A$ with $\mathrm{residue}_A(c)$ equal to the value at $s$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference of $g$ and the image of $c$ lies in $y$. Assume finally that $\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k_0\,q$, the $q$-fold expansion $j(\mathsf q^{q})$, lies in $K$ and in $C$, and that $a_0\in A\cap k_0$ satisfies $j(\mathsf q^{q})-a_0\in y$. Then, granted that the base change of $\mathrm{jq}$ is $R_0$-integral and that $a_0$ lies in $A$, the reduction of $a_0$ in $\kappa_A$ satisfies $\mathrm{residue}_A(a_0)^q = s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $j$.
--
--   This is the $H_1=\Gamma_0(M')\cap\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ ("Diamond") form of the statement that at a supersingular place the two branches of the level-$q$ modular correspondence are exchanged by Frobenius: the $j$-pin $j(\mathsf q^{q})$ of the chart reduces, modulo the maximal ideal $y$, to a $q$-th root of the supersingular value $\hat\jmath(s)$. It feeds the constructions of common charts, nodes and separating data for the Diamond case, and the classification of pinned $\Gamma_1$ Tate points.
